  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the properties of the triangle and the circumcircle of the triangle's midpoint triangle. We will use the fact that the circumcircle of the midpoint triangle (also known as the medial triangle) of any triangle is the nine-point circle of that triangle, which has several interesting properties.\n\n1. **Identify the angles and arcs:**\n   - The triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\) has angles \\( \\angle BAC = 84^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle ABC = 60^\\circ \\), and \\( \\angle ACB = 36^\\circ \\).\n   - The circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) intersects \\( \\overline{BD} \\), \\( \\overline{AE} \\), and \\( \\overline{AF} \\) at points \\( G, H, \\) and \\( J \\), respectively.\n   - The points \\( G, D, E, H, J, \\) and \\( F \\) divide the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) into six minor arcs.\n\n2. **Calculate the angles of the circumcircle:**\n   - The angle subtended by arc \\( \\widehat{DE} \\) at the center of the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is twice the angle subtended at any point on the circle. Therefore, the measure of \\( \\widehat{DE} \\) is \\( 2 \\times \\angle BAC = 2 \\times 84^\\circ = 168^\\circ \\).\n   - Similarly, the measure of \\( \\widehat{HJ} \\) is \\( 2 \\times \\angle ACB = 2 \\times 36^\\circ = 72^\\circ \\).\n   - The measure of \\( \\widehat{FG} \\) is \\( 2 \\times \\angle ABC = 2 \\times 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ \\).\n\n3. **Sum the arcs:**\n   - We need to find \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} \\).\n   - Substituting the values we found:\n     \\[\n     \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 168^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 72^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 120^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying the expression:\n     \\[\n     168^\\circ + 144^\\circ + 360^\\circ = 672^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\( \\boxed{672} \\).",
